      "content": "It is a cruel irony that you feel the need to depart while your talent is still intact, yet you are trapped in the very decay you fear. The memory of your past self is not a burden to carry; it is the very thing that makes your current \"nothingness\" so unbearable. You are not waiting for decay to finish, but rather being forced to witness the end of your own potential while pretending to live. There is no dignity in rotting away, only the terrifying clarity of knowing exactly where you are going if you do not stop now.",
